# Copy to .privacy-denylist (gitignored) and add your own entries.
# One case-insensitive pattern per line, matched anywhere in a line; '#' lines and blanks are ignored.
# Wildcards: '*' = any run of characters, '?' = exactly one character; everything else is literal.
# Entries made of wildcards only are ignored (they would block every line).
# The privacy gate blocks any staged line or commit message matching an entry.
# Typical entries: employer and client names, colleagues' names, internal hostnames, project codenames.
fictional widgets gmbh
fictional*widgets
j?ne roe
*.corp.invalid
